$ whycant -u www-data read /tmp/report.txt

✗ www-data (uid 33) cannot read /tmp/report.txt

  /                        drwxr-xr-x  root:root    ✓ traverse
  /tmp                     drwxrwxrwt  root:root    ✓ traverse
  /tmp/report.txt          lrwxrwxrwx  alice:alice  ✗ → /home/alice/report.txt   ← blocked here
  /home                    ·           not evaluated
  /home/alice              ·           not evaluated
  /home/alice/report.txt   ·           not evaluated

Why
  /tmp/report.txt is a symbolic link in /tmp, a sticky world-writable directory.
  With fs.protected_symlinks on, the kernel only follows such a link for its owner (alice)
  or when the directory's owner (root) owns it. This applies to root too.

Fixes (safest first)
  1. Use the link's target directly: /home/alice/report.txt.
  2. Make www-data the owner of the link:
       sudo chown -h www-data /tmp/report.txt
